> why name a stash container with a level name?

Not just containers, any item.  Naming items is one way of keeping
notes about the current dungeon.  You may want to remember
what level has the enterances to branches, what levels have shops.
You may want to record what color potions are what.

> You can't see it (and thus read the name) unless you're on that
> level anyway.

If you-the-player remember the level of your main stash and
you-the-character forgot information (amnesia, mindflayer), then
the informaton is preserved within the game.  Some like to take
notes.  Some consider storing stuff outside the game cheating.
People with both opinions will want to record notes within the
game.


